# Data conversion between gibibyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 0.0010TB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GiB yields 0.0016TB; backward, converting 1TB to 931.3225GiB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TB yields 1396.9838GiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
0.0010TB
0.0016TB
931.3225GiB
1396.9838GiB

<<< stderr
